    operand. Both were the same register, head + 1, so the compare
    could only match when another consumer had already moved head by
    one: the swap then succeeded and handed out a G that the other
    consumer had just taken. Two threads ran one routine, and the
    record was freed twice. %eax is the head we read; %edx is what we
    want it to become (P83). }
