    tail, copy n = len - len/2 entries into a batch on our stack, and
    only then move the victim's head with a CAS; a failed CAS discards
    the batch and starts over. Moving the head first and copying after,
    as this did, let the owner refill the very slots the thief had not
    copied yet (a queue index and the index 256 later share a slot), so
    two Ms ran one routine (P98). The batch goes straight to our tail:
    we steal only with an empty local queue. With an empty victim queue
    and the last spin round on (M+72), the victim's runnext is taken
    after a short wait. }
