  { rdi fd, rsi events, rdx milliseconds: rt_waitio2 with a deadline on
    the runtime's timers (P115, 1.1.1). It made a timerfd, armed it, put
    it on the epoll set and closed it, five system calls a wait where Go
    uses a timer of its runtime; a client with a deadline on each answer
    (dnsd's) paid 14% of the time. At most 2^40 ms, so the deadline
    cannot overflow; 0 or less returns 0 at once, the answer of a
    deadline that came, as Go answers pollErrTimeout at once for a
    deadline already past (runtime/netpoll.go, netpollcheckerr). P213: a
    bare ret gave back rax, the ms itself, so -7 read as an errno.
    xorl zero-extends into rax (SDM vol. 1, 3.4.1.1). }
