  { rt_gocallm (P342): rt_gocall for the heap's slow paths, which take
    more stack than a routine's first one keeps (PasHeapRefill's check
    asks 704 bytes, NewSpan's under it 912): from a routine's own stack
    they run on its M's system stack, r14 at the M's own record of it
    (rt_allg0, as Go's g0: its guard 24 KB below the stack's top, nothing
    preempted, never on the list of every record, never a collector
    worker's), as Go runs span allocation on the system stack
    (runtime/mheap.go alloc: systemstack, "Don't do any operations that
    lock the heap on the G stack"); elsewhere it is rt_gocall. None of these paths waits, so the M
    runs nothing else on its stack meanwhile, and the routine's own words
    stay where they are. Every register but rax kept. }
  Line('rt_gocallm:');
  Line('  testq %r14, %r14');
  Line('  jz rt_gocall');
  Line('  cmpl $5, 152(%r14)');
  Line('  je rt_gocall');
  Line('  cmpq 0(%r14), %rsp');
