{ rt_mapgetstr as on amd64 (1.0.69): x0 the map, x1 the key's two
  words; the value's slot in x0, or nil. The map, the key, H2 and the
  step wait in x19, x20, x22 and x23 across rt_xxh3, which touches no
  callee-saved register; x30 is saved, since the bl to it overwrites
  it. The fields are read at their widths (LDRB, LDRH, LDRSW, ARM DDI
  0487 M.c), and a small map's group whole (P285). }
procedure TEmitter.EmitMapGetStrArm;
begin
  Line('rt_mapgetstr:');
  Line('  cbz x0, .amg_nil');
